    803  f101							; +1 line/frame). Rows 0/1 now store+WSYNC before the tide block, then
    804  f101							; jmp over it (+3c charged to the FIRST body line = 66max+3jmp+3WSYNC
    805  f101							; = 72 <=76). Row2 path byte-identical in cost (cpx/beqT/lda/sta/WSYNC
    806  f101							; = 11+3 = 76, zero margin — the `beq` target is 9 bytes ahead, same
    807  f101							; page, T=3c; do not let this block grow toward a page edge).
    808  f101							; A1 gap fix (2026-10-05): `sta Temp` (+3c in .Row) pushed gaps to
    809  f101							; 77/79 = stall EVERY frame (265-line frames). `sta LineCount` moved
    810  f101							; AFTER `sta WSYNC` — same bytes, -3c from the gap window, +3c to the
    811  f101							; first body line (66max+3LC[+3jmp]+3WSYNC = 75 rows0/1, 72 row2).
    812  f101							; LineCount is not read until the line's `dec` tail — the early store
    813  f101							; was never required; keep the store strictly between WSYNC and .Line.
