    844  f120				   SliceReentry 		; global alias ON .Line — RowSlice's tail
    845  f120							;   jmp lands here (its scope can't see .Line)
    846  f120							; --- Player sprite: color for THIS line, graphics byte for NEXT line ---
    847  f120							; GRP0 written on line S displays on line S+1 (latched at the sprite's
    848  f120							; window start after the write) — index graphics with A0+1 ($ff wraps
    849  f120							; to 0 = row0 on the line before the sprite).
    850  f120							; Running-Y: Y = A0 = Scanline - RoomY is computed ONCE at kernel entry
    851  f120							; (sec/sbc RoomY/tay); .Line's iny advances it (Y = A0+1 after the
    852  f120							; graphics write = A0 of the next line). Nothing between rows may touch
    853  f120							; Y — the water-strip band-color read is an inlined `lda` (Y untouched).
    854  f120							; Cycle budget — MEASURED (sim_frame_budget, bugs.md #29 Class A):
    855  f120							; the old worst path (in-window color/beam/GRP0 + object in-range) was
    856  f120							; 78c: WSYNC write landed 2c into the next line -> full-line stall ->
    857  f120							; +1 scanline on every frame whose object window overlapped the A0=11
    858  f120							; line (24 stalls in the SIM_LEVEL=2 window, always even frames —
    859  f120							; SelectActiveObject parity rotation). Root fix: the color/beam gate
    860  f120							; below stops at A0=10; row 11 inherits row 10's COLUP0/ENAM0 writes
    861  f120							; (PlayerColTable/BeamMask [10]==[11], verify_build asserts) because
    862  f120							; GRP0 row11 is fetched on line A0=10 already ("row11 shows via
    863  f120							; line10"). Worst path measured 2026-10-15 (vcrunch jitter hunt):
    864  f120							; in-window color/beam/GRP0 + object in-range = 69c between WSs,
    865  f120							; start-to-start d=72 — was 73/76 (= stall zone 74-76, whole-screen
    866  f120							; +1-line jitter) until the dead `cpy #12 / bcs .GrpZero` (4c, never
    867  f120							; taken on the A0<=10 color path) moved to .GrpSkip. Budget: work
    868  f120							; <= 70c / d <= 73 — a 74-76 segment stalls a full scanline.
    869  f120							; ObjSprites+71 must stay in the $FExx page (else lda ObjSprites,X
    870  f120							; page-crosses, +1c on the GRP1 fetch) — verify_build enforces this.
    871  f120							; Branch targets all same-page (3c taken) and BeamMask operand in $FExx
    872  f120							; (4c fetch, no-cross — verify_build S2.2 guard).
    873  f120							; GRP1 object section clobbers X (ObjSprites index) — row counter lives in
    874  f120							; RowIdx and X is reloaded after bne. Row-advance +6c on the .Row setup
    875  f120							; scanline (segment 63c -> 69c <= 76c): frame length unchanged.
    876  f120							; The old Scanline/sec/sbc/tay prefix cost 10c more (body 66c -> WSYNC
    877  f120							; write on cycle 76 = one cycle late): WSYNC stalled a full line per
    878  f120							; overlapping scanline — stretched cave row, HUD pushed down, and with
    879  f120							; GRP1 flicker rotation the frame length alternated (one-tile oscillation).
    880  f120							; Keep the hot path at <= 70c work: an overrun duplicates the scanline.
    881  f120		       c0 0b		      cpy	#PLAYER_SPRITE_H - 1
    882  f122		       b0 49		      bcs	.GrpSkip	; A0 >= 11 (incl $ff): no color/beam this line.
    883  f124							; A0=11 skips too (Class-A stall line): rows
    884  f124							; 10/11 share color+beam bytes, so row 10's
    885  f124							; writes are still in effect here.
